{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.4,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 is scheduled as a 24k resistor across VOUTN and VOUTP, but its sourcing fields describe a 24Ω part: the description reads \"24Ω 0805 ... ±5%\" and the MPN FRC0805J240TSD encodes 24Ω. The schematic value and the purchased part disagree by three orders of magnitude.",
      "expected": "A 24k (about 24.9k) resistor across the PoE rectifier output, as the value field states, with a matching purchasable part. A 24Ω part across a roughly 50 V rail would dissipate on the order of 100 W.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(value \"24k\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R36 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"}
      ],
      "impact": "If built from the sourced part, the PoE-side resistor would be 24Ω instead of about 24k, loading the rectified supply heavily and likely failing the resistor. Detection or signature behaviour would also be wrong.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D14", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D14.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "The anodes of D4, D14 and D23 sit on net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW, and no other component pin is on that net. No supply, switch or driver connects to it, unlike the parallel LED-power net /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV, which is driven.",
      "expected": "Indicator LEDs need an anode supply. The LED-power net should connect to a rail or a switch, as the net name implies.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") (class \"Default\")\n      (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet activity LEDs (D14, D23) and the Pi activity LED (D4) would never light, removing status indication.",
      "confidence": 0.25
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist and SPICE deck agree on the main connectivity. The strongest deviation is R36, whose value (24k) contradicts its 24Ω description and MPN, and a secondary concern is the unpowered LED anode net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW; both are moderate-confidence."
}

